 24pp above the Real Estate median (23%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","It captures 2.34x its revenue share in sector profits, taking a disproportionate slice of the profit pool.","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 145 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 14% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 16% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 37% and a beta of 1.05, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.17 vs 5y 1.07), so read it loosely.","About $17.6M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 57% in the 2020 crash and 64% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $45.37 (margin of safety -21%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 35%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Real Estate peers: P/E 12.3 vs 23.6 and EV/EBITDA 10.9 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 45% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 5.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 5 covering analysts target $61.45 on average, 12% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.50).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.68x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 75%.","ROE of 6% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 3.8% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.7x net debt to EBITDA ($47.6M of cash against $393.7M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 6.1x.","Its debt comes due soon (maturity wall about 0.9 years out), so refinancing terms matter."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -1.3% over 3 years and 17.9% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 76%).","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 12.3% a year over five years.","Capex runs 6.5x depreciation (92.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.0%, and institutions hold 79%.","Insider trading is two-way: 2 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $996K bought.","It returns 15.6% a year to shareholders (1.3% in buybacks and 13.9% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.5% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It pays out 171% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk.","Short interest is elevated at 19.8% of the float, 7.6 days to cover."],"people":["With about 23 employees, each generates about $11.6M of revenue, 5.1x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 59.3% a year.","CEO pay is $2.3M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $441K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":52,"head":"Avoid: priced 21% above its fair value of $45.37.","pros":["Revenue grew 17.9%/yr over 5y","P/E 12.3x vs sector 23.6x","EV/EBITDA 10.9x vs sector 16.3x","Insiders net buyers ($996K over 12 months)","12-1 month momentum +14%"],"cons":["Trades 21% above fair value of $45.37","ROIC 8.0% vs WACC 8.7%"],"flags":["Priced 21% above its fair value of $45.37"],"need":[],"buy_below":38.56,"vc":{"base":45.37,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":45.37,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.3518,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (35% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"IIPR","date":"